WEBVTT

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:12.950
H-Hey, wait, Masumi!

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:15.660
I haven't finished changing or washed my face--

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.250
Shut it.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:25.160
One, two, three, four...

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:30.040
Five, six, seven, eight...

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:31.200
Step back.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:32.660
Okay.

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:35.410
Switch places then cross swords.

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:38.580
Again but speed it up.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.660
Whoa!

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:46.330
Ow...

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:51.620
We'll go at a speed you can keep up with.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.620
Thanks!

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:06.330
Masumi's affectionate <i>dere </i>side!

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:09.000
Masumi's teaching him?

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.910
Look at them go.

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:13.790
Was there a special event?

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:16.370
I discovered a hidden choice.

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:18.620
Seriously? Hell yeah.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:26.450
That was good.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:05.120
"On Love - Spring Edition"
Thanks, Masumi.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:07.120
"On Love - Spring Edition"
It was nothing. Didn't want him
to keep holding us back.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.870
It was nothing. Didn't want him
to keep holding us back.

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:15.200
You'll make it for the performance at this rate.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:16.580
You really think so?

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:19.450
As long as you don't overdo it.

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:23.700
Keep teaching him, Masumi.

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:24.910
Okay.

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:26.500
Thanks, Masumi!

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:28.200
I'll do my best!

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:30.660
--Let's keep at it together!

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:31.080
--Oh yeah.
--Let's keep at it together!

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:32.500
--Oh yeah.
--Get off.

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:35.910
How are ticket sales going?

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:38.790
Not to worry!

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:41.750
I've already publicized it
on our troupe's official site!

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:44.160
I didn't realize we had an official site.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:45.910
Wow, I wanna see it.

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:48.160
Don't get your hopes up...

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:51.040
"Click here to learn more about our troupe!"
"Mankai Company"
"Mankai Company Homepage"
"Site visited 33 times."

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:53.870
What do you think?

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:56.500
--It's like a site from ancient times.
--So lame.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:58.870
It'd be immediately removed in my country.

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:01.620
Oh yeah, the flyers were pretty bad, too.

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:06.370
I sorta know a graphic designer
who can make flyers and web sites.

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:07.200
Really?

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:11.370
He was a year ahead of me
in high school. I guess could ask...

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:13.000
You sound hesitant.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:17.450
We weren't close or anything...
I'll still ask, though.

00:04:17.450 --> 00:04:19.370
Thanks!

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:20.450
Is this site really that bad?

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:23.450
"Mankai Company Homepage"
"Site visited 33 times."
Is this site really that bad?

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:29.160
One, two, three, four...

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:33.580
Five, six, seven, eight...

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:36.080
That's enough for today.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:38.700
Review the adjustments we made today.

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:41.040
Yes, ma'am. Thank you!

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:42.160
Later.

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:44.950
Later, gator.

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:46.790
Director.

00:04:46.790 --> 00:04:50.200
I talked to the friend I mentioned
this morning about the troupe.

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:52.910
He's interested and said he'll stop by.

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:56.700
Really? Think he's interested in acting, too?

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:58.910
Uh... I dunno.

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:02.410
I see. Around what time will he come by?

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:04.700
Er, well...

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:06.080
Hi there!

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:08.120
Sounds like he's here.

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:11.830
Wow! What's this?

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:25.500
It's huge! It's my first time
standing on stage ever! This is wild!

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:26.540
Is that him?

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:28.250
He's stealing my spotlight!

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:29.160
So annoying.

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:31.700
Heya, Tsuzuroon. Haven't seen you in forever!

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:32.870
Tsuzuroon?!

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:35.000
Just ignore that.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:38.250
Wow, you're legit part of a theater troupe.

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:39.200
Tsuzuru?

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:43.700
Right, er, this is my friend, Kazunari Miyoshi.

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:45.540
Hi there.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:47.750
I'm Tachibana of Mankai Company.

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:50.950
Would you be able to help
design our site and flyer--

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:52.750
--Roger that!
--Huh?

00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:54.950
Tsuzuroon's filled me in already. I'm all in.

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:57.410
Anyways, I'll get my designs to you pronto.

00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:59.450
R-Right...

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:02.950
I'll get a bunch of my crew
to come watch, so good luck!

00:06:02.950 --> 00:06:05.660
Th-Thanks.

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:09.250
The lead actor and others
enter from here, huh? That's sick!

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:11.370
--Thee. Thy. Thou.
--He's actually a good person, so don't worry.

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:13.080
--Whatcha doin'?
--He's actually a good person, so don't worry.

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:16.700
Hero comes to save the day!
Something like that? Yeah?

00:06:16.700 --> 00:06:18.040
<i>So </i>annoying.

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:20.660
We agree for once.

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:21.580
"Mankai Company"

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:26.160
Wow!

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:27.450
This is how it looks now.

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:29.830
Jumped forward 20 years.

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:32.200
Raking in the views!

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:34.700
Despite his personality, he's got the skills.

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:38.040
Our website's improved. Let's do the same
by working hard at rehearsals!

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:40.160
Yeah!

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:46.000
Julius, listen to me!

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:50.080
Romeo, why do you have to be Romeo Montague?

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:53.000
Forsake your home and name, Julius.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:57.080
Don't we have an even grander dream to share?!

00:06:57.080 --> 00:07:01.540
I can't. I can't forsake my family.

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:03.500
Masumi.

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:06.200
Can you try that line again?

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:10.790
I can't. I can't forsake my family.

00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:15.910
Hm, I'm not getting
any feeling in just this line.

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:19.790
Try saying it with your own family in mind.

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:24.000
I was always alone at home.

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:28.500
I completed the special task you assigned me.

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:29.620
"Masumi"
"Find an actor you like"
I completed the special task you assigned me.

00:07:29.620 --> 00:07:31.000
"Masumi"
"Find an actor you like"

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:35.620
I can see the results.

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:40.290
You found an actor you like?

00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:41.450
Yeah.

00:07:41.450 --> 00:07:46.830
Imagine how that actor would
deliver that line and try it again.

00:07:46.830 --> 00:07:48.120
Okay.

00:07:52.870 --> 00:07:56.910
I can't. I can't forsake my family.

00:07:56.910 --> 00:08:00.410
Good. Your intonation was better this time.

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:06.620
It'll get way better if you can truly feel
those emotions while delivering that line.

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:09.330
It's not good enough.

00:08:09.330 --> 00:08:13.500
I just know that <i>you </i>can do better than that.

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:16.120
If you say so...

00:08:17.540 --> 00:08:22.620
Ta-dah! Look, everyone, the costumes are ready!

00:08:28.370 --> 00:08:29.370
They're amazing!

00:08:29.370 --> 00:08:31.080
Fits just right.

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:34.830
You're as good as a pro even though
you're a middle schooler.

00:08:34.830 --> 00:08:38.790
Of course I am. I'm going to make sure
they fit, so try moving around.

00:08:38.790 --> 00:08:41.750
It's a little tight at the waist.

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:42.700
Lose weight.

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:44.540
Aren't you fitting them to us?

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:46.580
You guys look great!

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:50.790
Yeah! Really feels like we're
getting closer to our performance!

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:55.120
So how many tickets have you sold?

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:56.870
Huh?

00:08:56.870 --> 00:08:58.330
Four tickets?!

00:08:58.330 --> 00:09:01.450
Me, Tetsuro, Yuzo, Kamekichi...

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:03.410
Kamekichi doesn't count!

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:04.580
Fail alert.

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:07.410
Our debut show will also be our final show!

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:11.120
I want more people to know about Mankai Company!

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:13.830
Let's do some advertising!

00:09:13.830 --> 00:09:15.750
I guess I can...

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:17.370
"Taruchi"
"Game Live Streamer.
Gather, Knights of the Round Table!"

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:20.250
I can advertise on my SNS account.

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:22.790
Whoa, you have over 50K followers!

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:24.450
So many!

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:29.370
We can also start a troupe blog
so people can get to know us.

00:09:29.370 --> 00:09:31.540
Itaru, can I leave that to you?

00:09:31.540 --> 00:09:32.410
Yeah.

00:09:32.410 --> 00:09:34.370
I'll help.

00:09:34.370 --> 00:09:39.450
I'll talk to Miyoshi about it, too.
He knows a bunch of people.

00:09:39.450 --> 00:09:40.870
--We'll go hand out flyers.

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:41.700
--I'm a good-for-nothing.
--We'll go hand out flyers.

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:43.330
--I'm a good-for-nothing.
--Yes, ma'am!

00:09:43.330 --> 00:09:47.750
--The official site was outdated and--
--I'll take a show ticket. And some flyers.

00:09:47.750 --> 00:09:48.830
Huh?

00:09:48.830 --> 00:09:52.700
I want a lot of people to see
the costumes I worked hard to make.

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:54.830
--I'll help advertise.
--Ah, an angel!

00:09:54.830 --> 00:09:57.200
Thanks, Yuki!

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:05.370
Please come watch <i>Romeo and Julius</i>,
presented by Mankai Company's Spring Troupe!

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:08.080
Please come watch!

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:10.620
Not many takers.

00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:13.950
Veludo Way is packed with theater troupes.

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:17.290
We need something unique to draw people in.

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:22.410
M-Masumi?

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:32.700
Romeo... Romeo Montague?

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:38.410
I don't believe it. Are you really
Romeo of House Montague?

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:47.620
Julius, are you really of House Capulet?

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:48.700
What's going on?

00:10:48.700 --> 00:10:50.000
<i>Romeo and Juliet</i>?

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:51.370
Isn't that <i>Romeo and Juliet</i>?

00:10:51.370 --> 00:10:53.160
They're both guys, though.

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:54.870
Looks interesting.

00:10:54.870 --> 00:10:56.540
We're Mankai Company.

00:10:56.540 --> 00:10:58.080
--Please come watch!
--Let's check it out!

00:10:58.080 --> 00:10:58.950
Yeah!

00:10:58.950 --> 00:11:00.580
Come watch. Come watch.

00:11:00.580 --> 00:11:01.410
Excuse me...

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:02.370
Yes?

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:03.750
Can I have one?

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:06.040
Of course. Here you go.

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:08.250
"Recruiting New Troupe Members"

00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:10.250
"Recruiting New Troupe Members"
Thank you very much.

00:11:12.910 --> 00:11:16.750
What? <i>Romeo and Juliet </i>with two guys?

00:11:16.750 --> 00:11:18.830
That's weird.

00:11:19.540 --> 00:11:21.910
"Recruiting New Troupe Members"
Please come watch if you'd like.

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:24.910
Thanks.

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:29.290
Romeo, why do you have to be Romeo Montague?

00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:31.870
Forsake your home and name, Julius.

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:36.160
Don't we have an even grander dream to share?!

00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:38.410
I can't. I--

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:46.370
What happened?

00:11:46.370 --> 00:11:48.290
That's it?

00:11:54.700 --> 00:11:58.950
We passed out most of
our flyers thanks to you two.

00:11:58.950 --> 00:11:59.790
I...

00:11:59.790 --> 00:12:02.450
The part you couldn't do will be fine
by the actual performance

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:04.700
if you keep practicing.

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:06.160
"Theater Blog"
"RowMeOh and JewLeeEss" "Citron"
Row-Me-Oh and Jew-Lee-Ess!

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:08.080
"RowMeOh and JewLeeEss" "Citron"
Row-Me-Oh and Jew-Lee-Ess!

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:10.250
Row-Me-Oh and Jew-Lee-Ess!

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:11.950
"RowMeOh and JewLeeEss!"
Row-Me-Oh and Jew-Lee-Ess!

00:12:11.950 --> 00:12:14.500
Yep, full of typos.

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:16.830
Itaru! Citron!

00:12:16.830 --> 00:12:18.500
What is it, Tsuzuru?

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:19.790
L-Look!

00:12:19.790 --> 00:12:20.250
"Have ideas for troupe publicity?"
"TV!"
"Get on TV!"
L-Look!

00:12:20.250 --> 00:12:22.540
"Have ideas for troupe publicity?"
"TV!"
"Get on TV!"
Miyoshi sent this!

00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:23.790
"TV!"

00:12:23.790 --> 00:12:26.040
"TV!"
TV?

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:27.790
"Scoop! Charming Neighbors Around Town"

00:12:28.500 --> 00:12:32.120
Hello! Today, I'm here at the
rehearsal studio of Mankai Company,

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:35.250
a long-established theater troupe
highly regarded by a select few.

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:39.580
Let's first have a word from the two leads.

00:12:39.580 --> 00:12:42.160
Th-Th-Th-Th-Thank for having us!

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:44.080
Way too nervous.

00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:47.370
I hear your friendship is
the main theme of the play?

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:53.540
Y-Y-Y-Yes, we're totally in sync! Right, Masumi?

00:12:55.160 --> 00:12:57.160
Looks like a TV blooper.

00:12:57.160 --> 00:13:04.790
I-It was tough 'cause we all just met,
but I-I was able to finish the script.

00:13:04.790 --> 00:13:07.660
You're one to talk.

00:13:07.660 --> 00:13:10.660
Wow, you're quite handsome.

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:14.370
Thank you. Since we're an all-male troupe,

00:13:14.370 --> 00:13:18.160
our performance will be especially
enjoyable to our female audience.

00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:22.120
Look at mature Itaru.
Can't tell he's actually a gamer bum.

00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:24.790
I'm Citron. I play the priest!

00:13:24.790 --> 00:13:26.790
When did you put a mask on?

00:13:26.790 --> 00:13:28.660
I could not be filmed without makeup.

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:30.200
You a girl?!

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:32.500
I hope this helps with publicity.

00:13:32.500 --> 00:13:33.950
Yes, me too.

00:13:33.950 --> 00:13:37.370
We've to thank Kazunari for his connections
with the TV broadcast company.

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:42.330
Oh?

00:13:43.410 --> 00:13:45.290
Good morning.

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:49.000
Morning, Chigasaki.

00:13:52.700 --> 00:13:56.580
I saw you on TV yesterday.
You joined a theater troupe?

00:13:56.580 --> 00:14:01.700
Yes, I did. Buy a ticket for my show.

00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:04.330
I will eventually.

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:17.580
It'll get way better if you can truly feel
those emotions while delivering that line.

00:14:20.450 --> 00:14:22.120
Masumi?

00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:29.950
Thanks for carrying that.

00:14:29.950 --> 00:14:31.370
Yeah.

00:15:00.450 --> 00:15:01.540
Hey...

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:03.160
Hm?

00:15:03.160 --> 00:15:06.080
How am I doing recently?

00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:10.080
How are you doing? You're doing good.

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:11.500
Really?

00:15:11.500 --> 00:15:15.580
Your sword fighting is progressing smoothly.
Remember how Yuzo said so, too?

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:18.290
Don't care what that old geezer says.

00:15:18.290 --> 00:15:21.080
I'm doing this for you.

00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:23.290
For me?

00:15:24.750 --> 00:15:27.330
That won't work.

00:15:27.330 --> 00:15:33.200
You should find a goal that will directly
help you grow rather than seek my praise.

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:39.290
Hey, isn't that Masumi?

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:42.370
OMG! Masumi, I saw you on TV!

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:43.620
Can I shake your hand?

00:15:43.620 --> 00:15:47.910
I bought tickets to your play.
I'm inviting my friends, too.

00:15:47.910 --> 00:15:48.950
Go away.

00:15:48.950 --> 00:15:50.790
Masumi!

00:15:50.790 --> 00:15:53.700
Who's the hag? His manager?

00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:54.700
Hag--

00:15:54.700 --> 00:15:57.290
I'm the director of his theater troupe.

00:15:57.290 --> 00:16:00.200
Really? This hag's the director?

00:16:00.200 --> 00:16:03.950
Do you think she's doing it
to get close to Masumi?

00:16:03.950 --> 00:16:05.080
What?

00:16:05.080 --> 00:16:06.830
Total abuse of power!

00:16:06.830 --> 00:16:09.330
Ugh, she's so old.

00:16:09.330 --> 00:16:11.200
That's not--

00:16:13.620 --> 00:16:17.620
Don't get too close Masumi, <i>hag</i>.

00:16:21.910 --> 00:16:24.450
Why you--

00:16:24.450 --> 00:16:25.620
No!

00:16:34.450 --> 00:16:37.910
Huh? What happened, Director?

00:16:37.910 --> 00:16:40.580
Nothing, really.

00:16:40.580 --> 00:16:44.450
Sorry, I didn't mean to--

00:16:44.450 --> 00:16:47.160
Huh? M-Masumi?

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:02.450
It's weird for him to get so depressed.

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:04.620
Did he get into an argument with the director?

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:07.700
Will Masumi be okay?

00:17:09.620 --> 00:17:15.450
I thought I got closer to Masumi.

00:17:15.450 --> 00:17:18.120
It's not that simple.

00:17:18.120 --> 00:17:24.080
We all just met and
don't know much about each other.

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:30.120
It's the same for Masumi. He just met us.

00:17:30.120 --> 00:17:36.540
Our friendship will continue
for a long time yet.

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:45.120
Masumi, I'm coming in.

00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:49.160
Tell us what happened already.

00:17:49.160 --> 00:17:51.330
Masumi, jeer up.

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:52.750
"Cheer up," right?

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:55.250
It'll just get worse if you hold it in.

00:17:55.250 --> 00:17:57.200
Masumi...

00:17:58.830 --> 00:17:59.870
Just kill me.

00:17:59.870 --> 00:18:02.160
--What?!
--What happened?!

00:18:02.160 --> 00:18:05.620
There's no point in living. I got dumped.

00:18:05.620 --> 00:18:08.620
Did you confess your love to the director?

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:09.540
No.

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:11.870
Does she have a lover?

00:18:11.870 --> 00:18:13.080
I'd kill--

00:18:15.580 --> 00:18:17.580
I'd kill them first!

00:18:17.580 --> 00:18:20.120
Hang on a sec. Calm down!

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:27.040
What happened?

00:18:28.700 --> 00:18:32.330
I wouldn't call that getting dumped.

00:18:32.330 --> 00:18:37.750
Just a misunderstanding. You assume
negative things in one-sided love.

00:18:37.750 --> 00:18:41.200
Having unrequited love is actually the best.

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:43.160
You sound so mature.

00:18:43.160 --> 00:18:45.620
Can't play as many games
if you're actually dating.

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:47.830
You sound like a hardcore gamer.

00:18:47.830 --> 00:18:50.000
You should talk it out with her.

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:52.330
Dunno what I should say.

00:18:52.330 --> 00:18:55.660
Just apologize.
Say you're sorry for hitting her.

00:18:55.660 --> 00:18:57.370
She hates me now.

00:18:57.370 --> 00:19:01.120
She'll forgive you. I'll go with you!

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:08.540
Sakuya sorta feels like the older brother here.

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:10.200
--Huh?
--True.

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:11.910
Masumi is little brother.

00:19:11.910 --> 00:19:16.160
Little brother? I don't have siblings,
so that's kinda nice.

00:19:16.160 --> 00:19:18.500
I'll go by myself.

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:20.700
Wait, Masumi!

00:19:25.660 --> 00:19:27.160
What's up?

00:19:28.080 --> 00:19:29.700
Go on.

00:19:29.700 --> 00:19:33.830
Sorry for hitting you earlier.

00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:38.160
It's fine, don't worry about it.

00:19:38.160 --> 00:19:39.410
You're not mad?

00:19:39.410 --> 00:19:44.290
Nope. You hit me accidentally,
because you were angry for my sake, right?

00:19:44.290 --> 00:19:50.160
Actually, I thought you were
worried about what I said.

00:19:50.160 --> 00:19:54.870
I don't know why I'm acting anymore.

00:19:54.870 --> 00:20:01.290
Your acting is getting better,
so I thought you found an actor you like.

00:20:01.290 --> 00:20:04.950
There was always someone whose acting I liked.

00:20:04.950 --> 00:20:07.580
Your acting.

00:20:07.580 --> 00:20:13.290
I love your acting, so I was just
doing my best like you.

00:20:14.620 --> 00:20:17.040
You like my terrible, hammy acting?

00:20:17.040 --> 00:20:18.830
That doesn't matter.

00:20:21.660 --> 00:20:24.370
Thanks, Masumi.

00:20:24.370 --> 00:20:25.500
What for?

00:20:25.500 --> 00:20:30.160
I thought I made no impression
on anyone as an actor.

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:31.910
That's not true.

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:38.160
Thank you for loving my acting.

00:20:40.160 --> 00:20:41.870
I love you.

00:20:44.250 --> 00:20:45.370
I love you.

00:20:45.370 --> 00:20:47.700
Er... Wait--

00:20:47.700 --> 00:20:49.450
Ahh!

00:20:49.450 --> 00:20:51.540
You can't, Masumi! Stop!

00:20:51.540 --> 00:20:52.700
Sakuya, you're in my way.

00:20:52.700 --> 00:20:54.450
You can't force her--

00:20:54.450 --> 00:20:57.120
W-Wait, what?

00:20:57.120 --> 00:20:59.540
Did you just call me by my name?

00:20:59.540 --> 00:21:01.080
He did!

00:21:01.080 --> 00:21:03.120
It's the first time you've used my name!

00:21:03.120 --> 00:21:05.120
Shut it.

00:21:08.450 --> 00:21:10.250
That makes me so happy, Masumi! Thanks!

00:21:10.250 --> 00:21:11.330
Call me by my name again!

00:21:11.330 --> 00:21:13.540
--Again! Come on!
--Get off me.

00:21:13.540 --> 00:21:14.950
Again!

00:21:14.950 --> 00:21:19.200
We in the Spring Troupe
started off as small flower buds.

00:21:19.200 --> 00:21:20.120
"Dress Rehearsal"

00:21:20.120 --> 00:21:21.500
"Dress Rehearsal"
We've grown and are waiting for that moment.

00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:23.830
"Will-Call for Invited Guests"
We've grown and are waiting for that moment.

00:21:24.790 --> 00:21:28.500
I'm sure we'll...

00:21:35.660 --> 00:21:38.370
Forsake your home and name, Julius.

00:21:38.370 --> 00:21:42.450
Don't we have an even grander dream to share?!

00:21:42.450 --> 00:21:49.120
I can't. I can't... forsake my family!

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:55.660
We will begin seating for
<i>Romeo and Julius </i>dress rehearsal shortly!

00:22:07.450 --> 00:22:14.120
I'm sure we'll go into full bloom on this stage!
